1
00:00:00,694 --> 00:00:01,890
When someone dies

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,897
the family inherits a phone queue.

3
00:00:04,497 --> 00:00:06,952
This is the machine that stands in it for them.

4
00:00:08,673 --> 00:00:11,614
The UK government automated its own half —

5
00:00:11,495 --> 00:00:13,793
one form tells every department.

6
00:00:13,823 --> 00:00:15,249
Then its website says:

7
00:00:15,129 --> 00:00:17,212
you'll also need to tell the banks

8
00:00:17,092 --> 00:00:18,810
the insurers, the pensions

9
00:00:18,689 --> 00:00:19,682
the utilities.

10
00:00:20,356 --> 00:00:21,951
Dozens of organisations.

11
00:00:22,091 --> 00:00:23,411
Days on hold.

12
00:00:23,416 --> 00:00:25,645
The death, retold to every single one.

13
00:00:27,219 --> 00:00:29,889
So the family talks to Afterward once.

14
00:00:29,944 --> 00:00:31,207
Margaret Rose Holt

15
00:00:31,087 --> 00:00:33,349
died on the thirteenth of September.

16
00:00:33,379 --> 00:00:35,208
Her son Daniel is the executor.

17
00:00:35,798 --> 00:00:37,381
And one thing matters here:

18
00:00:37,261 --> 00:00:39,243
the family has no account numbers.

19
00:00:39,243 --> 00:00:40,150
Remember that.

20
00:00:41,173 --> 00:00:42,568
Then it dials.

21
00:00:42,598 --> 00:00:44,086
Twelve institutions

22
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:46,672
in parallel — each card is a real recorded

23
00:00:46,552 --> 00:00:49,258
session with the AssemblyAI Voice Agent.

24
00:00:49,288 --> 00:00:51,608
It presses the menu keys itself.

25
00:00:51,638 --> 00:00:53,386
It waits through the hold music

26
00:00:53,266 --> 00:00:55,390
and says nothing until a human answers.

27
00:00:55,975 --> 00:00:57,160
Watch the timers:

28
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,224
that hold is real

29
00:00:58,104 --> 00:01:00,125
replayed at eight times speed.

30
00:01:03,219 --> 00:01:05,789
Here is the moment that matters most.

31
00:01:05,869 --> 00:01:07,166
At Harberton and Vale

32
00:01:07,046 --> 00:01:09,519
the agent tries to record an outcome before

33
00:01:09,399 --> 00:01:11,284
the clerk has issued a reference.

34
00:01:11,707 --> 00:01:14,377
The validator refuses its own agent.

35
00:01:14,382 --> 00:01:16,157
Refused, in red.

36
00:01:16,212 --> 00:01:18,748
It asks again, the clerk issues the reference

37
00:01:18,628 --> 00:01:20,772
and only a verified number is written.

38
00:01:21,347 --> 00:01:23,763
There is no code path that writes a guess.

39
00:01:25,693 --> 00:01:28,584
And when Wessex Building Society asks for something

40
00:01:28,464 --> 00:01:30,157
that isn't in the family's brief?

41
00:01:30,589 --> 00:01:32,060
The card turns amber.

42
00:01:32,115 --> 00:01:34,835
Needs you — with the exact question to answer.

43
00:01:34,914 --> 00:01:37,140
Meanwhile the seals keep landing:

44
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:38,870
Caledonia Life, case opened.

45
00:01:38,925 --> 00:01:40,592
Foxglove, case opened.

46
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:42,973
Verified reference numbers

47
00:01:42,853 --> 00:01:44,089
stamped one by one.

48
00:01:45,675 --> 00:01:48,371
Everything lands in the Estate Ledger.

49
00:01:48,425 --> 00:01:49,503
Per institution:

50
00:01:49,383 --> 00:01:50,870
the verified reference

51
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:52,511
the documents they asked for

52
00:01:52,390 --> 00:01:54,288
and the full stereo recording —

53
00:01:54,167 --> 00:01:56,339
the institution on the left channel

54
00:01:56,219 --> 00:01:57,637
Afterward on the right.

55
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:00,676
Evidence a solicitor can actually use

56
00:02:00,556 --> 00:02:02,003
shareable as one page.

57
00:02:04,223 --> 00:02:06,018
One thing we will not fake:

58
00:02:05,898 --> 00:02:08,651
the twelve institutions are a labelled

59
00:02:08,531 --> 00:02:09,848
scripted test bed.

60
00:02:09,902 --> 00:02:12,316
Calling a real bank with a fictional death

61
00:02:12,196 --> 00:02:14,348
would be fraud — so we refuse to demo it.

62
00:02:14,827 --> 00:02:17,490
Everything the agent did on those calls was

63
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:17,772
real.

64
00:02:19,744 --> 00:02:22,579
Six hundred and fifty thousand UK deaths a

65
00:02:22,459 --> 00:02:22,889
year.

66
00:02:22,944 --> 00:02:25,089
Around three million in the US.

67
00:02:25,144 --> 00:02:27,080
Every one of them creates this work.

68
00:02:28,673 --> 00:02:30,668
Tell Us Once covers government.

69
00:02:30,673 --> 00:02:33,341
The Death Notification Service covers member

70
00:02:33,221 --> 00:02:33,668
banks.

71
00:02:33,722 --> 00:02:36,272
Empathy and Settld do forms and email.

72
00:02:36,872 --> 00:02:38,442
Nobody makes the calls.

73
00:02:38,582 --> 00:02:39,636
That is the gap.

74
00:02:41,650 --> 00:02:43,625
The economics are measured

75
00:02:43,505 --> 00:02:44,431
not guessed.

76
00:02:44,486 --> 00:02:47,317
Twelve calls took twenty-eight minutes of agent

77
00:02:47,197 --> 00:02:49,756
time — two or three pounds of cost per estate.

78
00:02:49,835 --> 00:02:51,653
Sold through funeral directors

79
00:02:51,533 --> 00:02:53,286
who already package aftercare

80
00:02:53,166 --> 00:02:55,422
at seventy-nine to one-forty-nine per case.

81
00:02:57,248 --> 00:02:57,812
Next:

82
00:02:57,692 --> 00:02:59,478
the real phone leg.

83
00:02:59,533 --> 00:03:01,803
It starts with a call that harms no one —

84
00:03:01,683 --> 00:03:04,692
phoning real bereavement lines to ask one question:

85
00:03:04,572 --> 00:03:06,304
what do you need from a family?

86
00:03:06,804 --> 00:03:09,545
That map of requirements becomes the product's

87
00:03:09,424 --> 00:03:09,813
moat.

88
00:03:11,698 --> 00:03:12,443
Afterward.

89
00:03:12,578 --> 00:03:14,373
Built on AssemblyAI.

90
00:03:14,403 --> 00:03:17,102
Twelve calls, twelve verified references

91
00:03:16,982 --> 00:03:17,912
zero guesses.

92
00:03:18,483 --> 00:03:20,369
The calls after — made for you.
